+Title: CoreWeave — Signed Model & Evidence Pilot (Aegis)
+Duration: 8 weeks
+Goal: Demonstrate end-to-end trusted model lifecycle on CoreWeave: train on CoreWeave, sign with Aegis receipt_signer (Vault Transit), publish Rekor attestations, attach evidence bundle to model in MLflow, and serve only signed models on managed Triton. Deliver Panorama-style admin/reporting for attestation coverage and SLO dashboards.
+
+Success criteria / KPIs
+- Attestation coverage: >= 95% of promoted models in pilot have valid cosign+Rekor attestations.
+- Attestation latency: median signer roundtrip < 5s.
+- Serve enforcement: 100% of Triton model deployments in pilot validate signature before load.
+- Pilot conversion: at least one paid customer follow-up / PO.
+
+Scope & Deliverables
+- Infrastructure (CoreWeave): k8s namespace + PVs, MLflow, Triton, Vault (HA guidance), Rekor (Postgres), Prometheus/Grafana.
+- CI integration: GitHub Actions template (OIDC -> Vault), receipt_signer call, Rekor publish and evidence bundle generator.
+- Appliance/edge: simple agent (Go) that verifies attestation before loading model (for device/edge customers).
+- Admin UI: minimal dashboard showing model lineage, attestation status, SLOs & gatekeeper violations (Flask app).
+- Runbooks: operator deployment, signing key rotation, incident response.
+
+Milestones (8-week plan)
+- Week 0: Kickoff, define customer tenant, provision CoreWeave k8s target, allocate GPU quota.
+- Week 1: Provision MLflow, Triton, Prometheus. Deploy minimal Vault (HA recommended) and Rekor Postgres.
+- Week 2: Deploy receipt_signer (Vault Transit) and CI workflow; run a sample build to create attestation.
+- Week 3: Evidence bundle integration with MLflow; admin UI basic views.
+- Week 4: Triton enforcement webhook to validate cosign/Rekor before model load.
+- Week 5: End-to-end system test with sample model, attestation, Rekor entry and Triton serving.
+- Week 6: Onboard pilot customer(s), train one model on CoreWeave, follow CI->attest->deploy pipeline.
+- Week 7: Observability tuning, SLO dashboards, runbook validation, security checklist and pen-test readiness review.
+- Week 8: Pilot wrap, metrics report, conversion proposal.
+
+Risks & mitigations
+- Vault & key management: use KMS-backed auto-unseal where possible; if customer requires BYOK use dedicated Vault instance or transit to their KMS.
+- Rekor availability: deploy Postgres with backups and TLS ingress; use managed DB with automated snapshots.
+- Customer trust on keys: provide BYOK and option for customer-hosted Rekor.
+
+Acceptance
+- Deliverable sign-off: pilot customer confirms attestation evidence visible in asset metadata and model loads only when attested.
+
