+# Security & Compliance Checklist — CoreWeave Aegis Offerings
+
+Secrets & KMS
+- BYOK option: allow customer to mount their KMS key for Vault auto-unseal or use CoreWeave-provided KMS.
+- Vault in HA with auto-unseal; enable Kubernetes auth and Vault Agent sidecar for workloads.
+- Rotate signing keys (Transit) quarterly and test signature verification post-rotation.
+
+Rekor & Attestation
+- Rekor backed by Postgres (managed), TLS secured ingress via cert-manager.
+- Regular backups (daily snapshots), restore drills monthly.
+
+Network & Isolation
+- Tenant network segmentation (namespace + NetworkPolicy), private cluster endpoints, Egress policies for registry communications.
+- Image allowlist enforced by Gatekeeper policy templates.
+
+Data Protection & Privacy
+- Encrypted object storage (SSE-KMS).
+- Access logs and audit trails sent to MCP (governance).
+- For federated flows: document epsilon/delta budgets; require opt-in and retention policies.
+
+Operational Security
+- Periodic pentest (annual) and SCA (dependabot + trivy in CI).
+- RBAC reviews for admin roles; enforce least privilege.
+- Seccomp/AppArmor profiles for critical pods.
+
+Legal & Compliance
+- Provide BAAs where PHI is involved; prepare SOC2/ISO/FedRAMP roadmap if required by customers.
+- Maintain consent templates and data processing agreements for federated participants.
+
