*** Add File:RUNBOOK_deploy_coreweave.md
+# Runbook: Deploying Aegis Pilot on CoreWeave
+
+Prereqs
+- CoreWeave tenant with k8s cluster access, PVs and GPU quota (if Triton/train needed).
+- Secrets: S3 artifact bucket, Rekor DB creds, Vault KMS key or BYOK, MLflow DB credentials.
+
+Steps
+1. Create namespace: kubectl create ns aegis
+2. Deploy Rekor Postgres (or use managed DB); then apply k8s/rekor/rekor-postgres-deployment.yaml.
+3. Deploy Vault via Helm using helm/values-vault-coreweave.yaml; verify auto-unseal with KMS.
+4. Deploy receipt_signer configured to use Vault Transit (ensure VAULT_ADDR points to in-cluster service).
+5. Deploy MLflow (Helm) with mlflow-values-coreweave.yaml.
+6. Deploy Prometheus & Grafana or use CoreWeave monitoring.
+7. Deploy Panorama plugin (build/push aegis/panorama-plugin:latest) and create Service + Ingress.
+8. Configure GitHub Actions secrets: VAULT_ADDR, VAULT_OIDC_ROLE, RECEIPT_SIGNER_URL, REKOR_URL, S3 creds.
+9. Run CI sample workflow to produce attestation and evidence bundle (see .github/workflows/ci_pan_sign_attest.yml).
+10. Validate: MLflow shows model, evidence bundle attached; Triton enforcement accepts signed model.
+
+Testing & Validation
+- Test attestation: curl <receipt_signer>/sign with sample artifact -> verify Rekor entry.
+- Test Triton load: attempt to load unsigned model -> should be rejected by pre-load webhook.
+- Run SLO checks: verify Prometheus metrics for signer latency, attestation count, and model_load_success_total.
+
+Rollback
+- If attestation service fails, revert to manual approval workflow (A2A) and pause automatic deployments via Gatekeeper.
+
