+# Secure Aggregation & DP Guidance — CoreWeave Pilot
+
+Recommendations
+- Use a vetted secure aggregation library (TensorFlow Federated secure aggregation, OpenMined PySyft, or Meta SecAgg).
+- Enforce enrollment: Vault-issued short-lived tokens for participants; log participant lists to Rekor for non-repudiable audit.
+- Contribution clipping and anomaly detection prior to aggregation to avoid poisoning.
+- Apply DP after aggregation using vetted libs (diffprivlib or PyDP) and document epsilon/delta for customers.
+
+Testing
+- Simulate Byzantine clients and test aggregation correctness.
+- Privacy-utility evaluation: run multiple epsilon settings, measure model utility vs privacy.
+- Third-party security review and threat modeling prior to production launch.
